.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-record 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-record \- Out\-of\-tree verdict stores: what something else judged, keyed so a stale answer cannot answer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten record\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Out\-of\-tree verdict stores: what something else judged, keyed so a stale answer cannot answer
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-record\-tool(1)
Record a declared tool row\*(Aqs verdict, read as `<name> <token>` lines on stdin
.TP
batten\-record\-forge(1)
Record the forge\*(Aqs check verdicts for one commit, read as `<check> <conclusion>` lines on stdin
.TP
batten\-record\-plan(1)
Record this branch\*(Aqs plan, read as `<id> <status>` lines on stdin
.TP
batten\-record\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
